# Cloudflare Pages response headers.
#
# The site answers on three hostnames: the apex, www, and the Pages project's own
# way4tech-website.pages.dev. All three returned 200 with index,follow, so the
# preview host is a complete, indexable copy of the production site competing
# with it for the same brand queries.
#
# The rule below is scoped to the absolute preview URL on purpose. A bare /*
# would apply to every host and would noindex the real site. After deploying,
# confirm both of these:
#   curl -sSI https://way4tech-website.pages.dev/ | grep -i x-robots-tag  -> noindex
#   curl -sSI https://way4tech.com/ | grep -i x-robots-tag                -> nothing
#
# This cannot live in robots.txt: that file is served byte-identical on all
# three hostnames, so a Disallow there would block the apex too.
#
# www is NOT handled here. Redirecting it to the apex has to be a Redirect Rule
# in the Cloudflare dashboard, as public/_redirects already notes.
https://way4tech-website.pages.dev/*
  X-Robots-Tag: noindex, nofollow
